Changes in v6:
- get_base_stats() reports the retired-queue remainder so netdev-genl
  qstats and ndo_get_stats64 agree after ethtool -L shrinks the queue
  count
- implement struct netdev_stat_ops for standard per-queue
  packets/bytes/drops instead of private ethtool strings
- keep replenish_* as plain per-queue u64 rather than atomics; the
  adapter-wide ethtool -S keys are summed on read and no per-queue
  keys are added for them
- add a per-queue no_buffer_retired carry; adapter->rx_no_buffer was
  last-queue-wins once more than one RX queue ran, and could go
  backwards across a reopen
- do not add buffer-submit hypercall counters: which of the three
  hcalls a replenish batch picks is an implementation detail, not
  something worth a permanent ethtool key
- table-drive ethtool -S with enum ibmveth_stat_src, and derive the
  per-queue key counts with ARRAY_SIZE()
- drop the H_SEND_LOGICAL_LAN counter: it incremented once per
  successful send, which just duplicates tx_packets, and it was the
  only counter that needed a queue index plumbed into ibmveth_send()
- drop the three pool%d_ ethtool keys the v5 draft added. size and
  active duplicate the writable poolN/num and poolN/active sysfs
  attributes, and available is reported for every queue by the
  debugfs buffer_pools table instead of for queue 0 alone, so the
  keys were 15 entries of permanent ABI carrying nothing new
- gate ibmveth_reset() on netdev->reg_state == NETREG_REGISTERED so a
  queued reset worker cannot re-open an unregistered device

Changes in v5:
- Expose per-queue packet/byte counters via ethtool -S (v6 moves the
  standard packets/bytes/drops to netdev_stat_ops; -S keeps
  driver-specific counters only)
- Implement .ndo_get_stats64
- Fix remove teardown order: unregister_netdev before cancel_work_sync
- Clear vio drvdata before free_netdev on probe error
